    "updated_at": "2021-05-24T07:24:11Z",
    "body": "The WHATWG URL Standard internally stores components in a percent-encoded form, to make full URL serializing simpler (it's just string concatenation). That is already the _status quo,_ and not a focus of this issue.\r\n\r\nThough the original issue was phrased in terms of the JavaScript getters, it could equivalently be phrased as \"should `'` be percent-encoded in the serialized result (`new URL(...).href`)?\"",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
